var V516_GUIDE=[
['The basics','What is the Leave page for?','<p>It is where the office records, approves and follows everyone\u2019s leave: vacation, sick and casual. You can see who is off today, each person\u2019s balance, and every application and decision.</p>'],
['The basics','What are Staff members and Atlantic?','<p>The blue switch at the top chooses whose leave you are looking at. <b>Staff members</b> are the office staff. <b>Atlantic</b> are the people on the Atlantic shifts, whose days are counted by their shift cycle.</p><p>Each side has its own permission, so you may only see one of them.</p>'],
['The basics','What do Requests, Leave and By person show?','<ul><li><b>Requests:</b> applications people sent in the app. Waiting ones come first, then recent decisions.</li><li><b>Leave:</b> everyone\u2019s leave for the year, as a list or a calendar. The chips filter by type.</li><li><b>By person:</b> one person\u2019s leave, their balance, and how this year compares with last year.</li></ul>'],
['The basics','What do the four tiles mean?','<p><b>On leave now</b>, <b>On vacation</b>, <b>On sick leave</b> and <b>On casual leave</b> count the people who are off today. Tap a tile to see who they are.</p>'],
['The basics','What do the coloured pills mean?','<ul><li><b>On leave now:</b> off today. <b>Starts in 3 days:</b> not started yet. <b>Ended:</b> finished.</li><li><b>Ongoing:</b> sick leave with no last day yet.</li><li><b>Recorded:</b> saved by the office. <b>Approved:</b> an application that was approved.</li><li><b>Waiting</b> and <b>Changes asked:</b> an application still being handled.</li><li><b>Declined</b> and <b>Cancelled</b> are red. <b>Ended early:</b> the rest of the leave was cancelled.</li><li><b>Application needed</b> or <b>received:</b> the paperwork for a recorded sick leave.</li></ul>'],
['The basics','Where do I see all the details of one leave?','<p>Tap the leave anywhere: in Requests, in the Leave list, on a person\u2019s leave page, in Others on leave, or from a bell alert. It always opens the same Leave information page, with every detail and the same buttons at the bottom.</p>'],
['Recording leave','How do I record leave for someone?','<ol><li>Tap <b>+ Add</b> at the top.</li><li>Choose the person. You can search by name.</li><li>Choose vacation, sick or casual leave.</li><li>Set the first day, then the last day or the number of days.</li><li>Add a note if you need to, then tap <b>Save</b>.</li></ol><p>The leave is signed with your saved signature and gets a reference number.</p>'],
['Recording leave','What does Sick today do?','<p>It is a quick way to record sick leave that starts today. Choose the person and save. Everything else works like any recorded sick leave.</p>'],
['Recording leave','How are the days counted?','<p><b>Staff members:</b> Monday to Friday. Tick the Saturday or Sunday box if the person works weekends. You can also type the number of days yourself.</p><p><b>Atlantic:</b> only the person\u2019s shift days count. Their rest days are skipped.</p><p><b>Sick leave</b> (staff and Atlantic): every day counts, rest days, weekends and public holidays too. The day back at work is still the next working day or shift.</p>'],
['Recording leave','Someone called in sick and did not say for how long. What do I do?','<ol><li>Record the sick leave as usual and tick <b>Not known yet</b>.</li><li>The leave shows <b>Ongoing</b> and counts each day up to today.</li><li>When they are back, open the leave and tap <b>Back at work</b>, then choose their last day off.</li></ol><p>Any days over their allowance are worked out as without pay when you tap Back at work.</p>'],
['Recording leave','What is Days they asked for?','<p>Optional. It is only what the person said when they called. The days actually booked are set by the dates and the number of days.</p>'],
['Recording leave','What is Complaint given?','<p>Optional. What the person told you, for example a headache or back pain. It is printed on the sick leave record.</p>'],
['Recording leave','How do I keep a complaint private?','<p>Choose <b>Injury</b>, <b>Medical appointment</b> or <b>Other</b> (they show a lock), or type the symptoms: these are private. Only Executives and up can read them. Everyone else sees <b>Private (senior management only)</b>, and the letter says \u201CI was absent due to illness\u201D.</p>'],
['Recording leave','Who signs a recorded leave, and what name is shown?','<p>The person who saves it signs it with their saved signature. The record shows their name and their company position, for example Coordinator. If they have not been placed in a position yet, only their name is shown.</p>'],
['Recording leave','Why does saving ask for my signature?','<p>Every recorded leave is signed. Set up your signature once under My signature in Settings, and the app uses it each time you save.</p>'],
['Recording leave','What happens if the leave goes over the person\u2019s allowance?','<p>The days over the allowance are counted as days without pay. If you are not an Executive, the leave goes to an Executive as a waiting request instead of being saved straight away.</p>'],
['Recording leave','Why does it say the person already has leave on these days?','<p>Two leaves cannot cover the same day for one person. Open the leave that is already there and change it, or choose other dates.</p>'],
['Applications','What is an application?','<p>The person\u2019s own written request, with their signature. Leave they apply for in the app is an application. Sick leave the office records needs an application afterwards, so it shows <b>Application needed</b> until it arrives.</p>'],
['Applications','The person has the app. How do they apply?','<p>They apply under My profile and leave. Their application appears in Requests for a decision. When the office records sick leave for them, they are told to apply when they are back at work.</p>'],
['Applications','The person does not have the app. How do I deal with their leave?','<ol><li>Record the leave with <b>+ Add</b>.</li><li>When their paper form, email or message arrives, open the leave and tap <b>Application received</b>.</li><li>If they need a form, tap <b>Print blank form</b> so they can fill it in and sign it.</li></ol>'],
['Applications','What does Application received ask for?','<p>How you got it (paper form, email, message, in person or other), the date you got it, and a photo of the form if you have one.</p>'],
['Applications','How do I print a blank form?','<p>Open a leave that shows Application needed and tap <b>Print blank form</b>. The form already has the person\u2019s name and the leave on it.</p>'],
['Applications','Can I scan a paper form instead of typing it?','<p>Yes. In <b>+ Add</b>, tap <b>Scan it</b> next to Have a paper form?. The app reads the form and fills in the details. Check them, then save. It is saved straight away by you.</p>'],
['Applications','Where do I see the form or the record later?','<p>On the leave page: <b>View paper form</b> shows the photo, and <b>View PDF</b> shows the signed record you can download or print.</p>'],
['Approvals','Who approves leave?','<p>People who can manage leave approve requests for their side (Staff members or Atlantic). Executives can approve both. Nobody can approve their own leave.</p>'],
['Approvals','How do I approve or decline a request?','<ol><li>Open it from Requests.</li><li>Read the details and Others on leave in this period.</li><li>Use the decision card: <b>Approve</b>, or type a reason and tap <b>Decline</b>.</li></ol><p>If it goes over the allowance, you choose how many days are without pay before approving.</p>'],
['Approvals','Can sick leave be declined?','<p>No. Sick leave is recorded, not declined. You can <b>Record sick leave</b>, or <b>Ask for changes</b> if something is missing, for example an unreadable certificate.</p>'],
['Approvals','What does Ask for changes do?','<p>It sends the application back to the person with your note. It shows <b>Changes asked</b> until they fix it and send it again.</p>'],
['Approvals','Can someone take back their request?','<p>Yes, while it is still waiting. They withdraw it from My profile and leave, and it shows <b>Withdrawn</b>.</p><p>An Atlantic manager who recorded leave that is still waiting for an Executive can withdraw it too: open it from Requests and tap <b>Withdraw</b>.</p>'],
['Approvals','What do Recorded by and Decided by mean?','<p><b>Recorded by</b> is the person who saved the leave record. <b>Decided by</b> is the person who approved or declined the application. Both show the name and the company position.</p>'],
['Balances','How is the balance worked out?','<p>The person\u2019s allowance for the year, minus the days of that type already counted that year. The line under their name shows it, for example Sick 2026: 2 of 5 days used, 3 left.</p>'],
['Balances','What does without pay mean?','<p>Days taken over the allowance. They are still leave, but unpaid. They show on the leave page and are picked up by Payroll.</p>'],
['Balances','Where are the allowances set?','<p>Open the three-dots menu at the top, then <b>Leave allowances</b>. Only Executives can change allowances: the company defaults and each person\u2019s own numbers. Atlantic allowances are set by role and per person.</p>'],
['Balances','Why does it say no allowance is set?','<p>Nobody has set that type of allowance for the person yet. The days are still counted. Set the allowance under Allowances and the balance appears.</p>'],
['Balances','What is Balance after?','<p>How many days of that type the person has left after this leave.</p>'],
['Balances','Does each year start again?','<p>Yes. Balances are counted per calendar year. Use the year arrows to look at another year.</p>'],
['Changing and cancelling','How do I change a leave?','<p>Open the leave and tap <b>Change</b>. Edit it and save. It is signed again, keeps its reference number, and the PDF says Amended. The change shows on the leave page and in History.</p>'],
['Changing and cancelling','When can a leave be cancelled?','<ul><li><b>Not started yet:</b> tap <b>Cancel this leave</b>. All the days go back.</li><li><b>Started but not finished:</b> tap <b>Cancel the rest</b>.</li><li><b>Already taken:</b> it cannot be cancelled.</li></ul>'],
['Changing and cancelling','What does Cancel the rest do?','<p>Today counts as taken. From tomorrow, the remaining days go back to the person\u2019s allowance and the leave now ends today. It shows <b>Ended early</b>.</p>'],
['Changing and cancelling','Why can\u2019t I cancel a leave that has passed?','<p>Those days were taken and may already have been paid. Only days that have not come yet can be cancelled.</p>'],
['Changing and cancelling','What happens when a leave is cancelled?','<p>The days go back to the person\u2019s allowance straight away. The leave disappears from Requests, the lists, the tiles, the counts, the calendar and Others on leave. It is kept in History with a red Cancelled pill.</p>'],
['Changing and cancelling','Is the person told when their leave is cancelled?','<p>Yes. Staff members get a phone and bell alert when their leave is cancelled or the rest of it is cancelled.</p>'],
['Changing and cancelling','What is a locked month?','<p>On the 1st of each month, the month before is locked. A leave that started in a locked month cannot be changed or cancelled.</p>'],
['Changing and cancelling','Can a leave be deleted?','<p>No. A signed leave can only be cancelled, so there is always a record of it.</p>'],
['History','Where is the leave History?','<p>Open the three-dots menu at the top, then <b>Leave history</b>.</p>'],
['History','What does History show?','<p>Every leave event, newest first: recorded, changed (with what it was before), cancelled (who and why), ended early, back at work, applications and decisions. Search by name or reference, or use the chips to show one kind. Tap a line to open that leave.</p>'],
['History','Who can see History?','<p>The people who can manage leave on that side. Executives see both sides.</p>'],
['Who sees what','Who can see and manage leave?','<p>It is set in Access and permissions: <b>Leave: Staff members</b> and <b>Leave: Atlantic</b>, each None, View or Manage. Executives have both.</p>'],
['Who sees what','Who can see sensitive information?','<p>Executives and up. The person it is about can also see their own.</p>'],
['Who sees what','What can someone with View only do?','<p>See leave, balances and History for their side. They cannot add, change, cancel or approve anything.</p>'],
['Problems','Why can\u2019t I see the Change or Cancel buttons?','<ul><li>You have View only access.</li><li>The leave is already cancelled.</li><li>It started in a locked month (no Change).</li><li>It has already been taken (no Cancel).</li><li>It is ongoing sick leave: use <b>Back at work</b> instead.</li></ul>'],
['Problems','A person is missing from the list. Why?','<p>Staff members must be in Staff Members. Atlantic people must be on an Atlantic shift in the roster. Someone who was removed shows as Removed person on their old leave.</p>'],
['Problems','Why does no position show after a name?','<p>That person has not been placed in a company position in Access yet. Once they are, new records show their position.</p>'],
['Problems','Why does the PDF say Amended?','<p>The leave was changed after it was first signed. The page and History show what it was before.</p>']];
